From f1b39e2050e2e9061da1f46dd546e80597d5ac45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:26:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: test for granite, not granite-or-above, in the ranged
 move check

borg_danger_one_kill() simulates a fast monster taking one step before
it attacks.  The melee simulation treats a neighbouring grid as a wall
when it is granite, magma, quartz or rubble; the ranged simulation
tested feat >= FEAT_GRANITE instead of feat == FEAT_GRANITE.  The
features numbered above granite are permanent wall (already skipped
just before), lava and passable rubble, so lava and passable rubble
were also treated as walls that only pass-wall and kill-wall monsters
can enter.

So a fast spellcaster one step behind a pile of passable rubble, which
it can walk onto and cast from in the same turn, added no ranged danger
at all, and the borg took no precaution against it.

Test feat == FEAT_GRANITE, as the melee simulation does.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#68.
---
 src/borg/borg-danger.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-danger.c b/src/borg/borg-danger.c
index 11efe9f1a..305aa1e9c 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-danger.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-danger.c
@@ -2663,7 +2663,7 @@ int borg_danger_one_kill(
                 continue;
 
             /* Cannot occupy a wall/seam grid (unless pass_wall or kill_wall) */
-            if (borg_grids[y_temp][x_temp].feat >= FEAT_GRANITE
+            if (borg_grids[y_temp][x_temp].feat == FEAT_GRANITE
                 || (borg_grids[y_temp][x_temp].feat == FEAT_MAGMA
                     || borg_grids[y_temp][x_temp].feat == FEAT_QUARTZ
                     || borg_grids[y_temp][x_temp].feat == FEAT_MAGMA_K
